<title>AUSTRIA: Saudi oil minister says Iraq return &quot;market-determined&quot;.</title>
<headline>Saudi oil minister says Iraq return &quot;market-determined&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabian oil minister Ali bin Ibrahim al-Nuaimi said on Tuesday that the accommodation of Iraqi exports to the market was &quot;a market-determined activity.&quot;</p>
<p>Nuaimi was responding to reporters' questions on OPEC's role in the return of Iraq oil under the U.N. oil-for-food deal.</p>
<p>He declined to answer questions on any further issues facing the group at its meeting due to start on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Nuaimi had just completed a courtesy call on Qatari oil minister Abdullah bin Hamad al-Attiyah and later called on acting UAE oil minister Rakad bin Salem bin Rakad .</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
